{ Blocks nested past ADR-0020's limit.

  The parser bounds the tree it builds at 1000 levels, and Sema's scope stack
  is sized one deeper on the strength of it: `scopeMark` is
  `array [0..maxBlockDepth]` and the comment beside maxBlockDepth said every
  block "is reached through a declaration the parser counted".

  It was not. ParseBlock did not count, so a procedure declaration nested a
  scope without nesting the tree, and 1001 of them indexed scopeMark past its
  end -- the compiler stopped with `array index out of bounds (0..1001)` on
  stderr, where its diagnostics go to stdout, so a caller redirecting stderr
  saw a non-zero exit and no message at all.

  1001 is the first depth that did it; 1000 compiled clean. }
